                                        {
                                            "activity_type": "Review",
                                            "description": "Recall and review Senior 2, Topic 1."
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "activity_type": "Investigation",
                                            "description": "In pairs, consider the functions f(x) = 6x and g(x) = x + 5\n(a) What is f(3)?\n(b) What is g(f(3))?\n(c) What is g(3)? What is f(g(3))? Is g(f(3)) the same as f(g(3))?\n(d) What is f(f(5))=f^2 (5)?\nRepeat for x."
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "activity_type": "Investigation",
                                            "description": "Investigate the inverse function of a given function. Illustrate graphically. What do you notice? By considering the domain and range of the function and its inverse – explain why this happens."
                                        }
                                    ],
                                    "suggested_assessment_activities": [
                                        {
                                            "assessment_type": "Observation/Task",
                                            "description": "Observe the learners in their groups as they work on the tasks below. During the process, are learners communicating effectively? are they learning from one another? are they creative and critical?\n1. f(x) is the greatest number prime less than x. Find: (a) f(40), (b) f(29)\n2. If f(x) = 2x³ and g(x) = x – 1, find h(x)=f(g(x)). Find h⁻¹(x), and sketch the graph of function h with its inverse.\n3. Given f(x) = 2x and g(x) = x – 3, find;\n(a) f³(x) (b) f(x³) (c) g²(x) (d) g(x²) (e) gf(x) (f) f(g(x)) (g) f(g(f(x)))"
                                        }
                                    ],
