                                        {
                                            "activity_type": "Problem Solving",
                                            "description": "b) Bayo, Ruth and John were all born on Independence Day, but in different years. Bayo is one year older than Ruth. John’s age is 3 times Bayo’s age.\nIf Ruth is r years old, write down expressions for:\n(a) Bayo’s age\n(b) John’s age\n(c) How many years older than Bayo is John? Give your answer in terms of r\n(d) In 6 years’ time, John will be 6 years older than Bayo. How old is Ruth now?"
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "activity_type": "Exercise",
                                            "description": "a) Solve quadratic inequalities and represent the solutions on a number line."
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "activity_type": "Exercise",
                                            "description": "b) Extend graphing inequalities to include quadratics."
                                        }
                                    ],
