                                        },
                                        {
                                            "activity_type": "Practical/Hands-on",
                                            "description": "On a rectangular piece of paper, mark a point a few centimetres from the centre of one edge. Fold the edge to pass through the point multiple times – to obtain the envelope below.\nWhat shape is the locus? Prove it by adding a set of axes and using algebra."
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "activity_type": "Construction/Algebra",
                                            "description": "On a coordinate grid plot points A (2, 3) and B (-4, 7). Construct and find the equation of the perpendicular bisector of AB."
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "activity_type": "Problem Solving/Sketching",
                                            "description": "A goat is tethered to the corner of a building. Assuming the length of the rope is less than the length of the sides of the building, sketch the locus of the area the goat can reach. What if the rope is longer than one of the sides of the building? Both sides of the building? Construct the locus in each case."
                                        }
                                    ],
                                    "suggested_assessment_activities": [
                                        {
                                            "assessment_type": "Observation/Task",
                                            "description": "Observe the learners in their groups as they work on the tasks below. During the process, are learners communicating effectively? Are they learning from one another? Are they creative and critical?\n1. Sketch and describe the locus of point M, where M is the mid-point of a chord of length 6 cm in a circle of radius 5 cm.\n2. Find the equation of the locus of P such that AP is 5 units, where A is (2, 3).\n3. Construct the locus to show the area available to a cow tethered by a rope of 3m to a horizontal rail length 4m.\nWhat is the area of the locus?"
                                        }
